members.doc:
Register command + parse chord + bind the callback in the global list.
Returns false (and registers nothing) if the chord string does not parse;
an empty chord string registers a command with no keybind.

How many arrange bodies ran, and how many were skipped. The layout
tests pin that a second pass over an unchanged tree arranges nothing;
a wall-clock delta would prove nothing on a loaded machine.

A long-running task's card. While Progress returns [0, 1) the card
stays up with a bar and LiveBody (when set) replaces Body each frame;
at 1 it times out like any toast, and below 0 it closes at once.

Create from an existing platform window. Arc renders into it but doesn't own it.
Set createSwapchain=false when the host engine owns the swapchain (UE5-style);
externalColorFormat must then match the host's render-target format.

Framework context menu (U1): dismisses open menus, builds an AMenu
from the entries and anchors it at the given window-space point,
clamped to the window. The boilerplate every panel used to carry.

types.doc:
The window the virtualizer instantiated. Rows are one half-open span;
columns are TWO, because the frozen ones are resident whatever the
horizontal scroll is and the rest are not.
